Make the third-party speaker feature bit advertisable

Senders pick the AirPlay-picker icon in two steps: an Apple model
string (e.g. "AudioAccessory5,1") maps to that product's icon, and
otherwise a receiver advertising feature bit 26 (Authentication_8,
MFi) - or bit 51 - is classified ThirdPartySpeaker and drawn with the
bookshelf-speaker icon. Anything else gets the plain generic glyph,
regardless of the model string (verified with synthetic mDNS
registrations against iOS; Sonos and WiiM receivers advertise bit 26).

shairport-sync hardcodes the features mask without bit 26. New option:
general.airplay_third_party_speaker, default off (mask unchanged).
Companion to 0001 (general.airplay_device_model); carried locally by
boompi.

--- a/common.h	2026-08-06 02:40:48
+++ b/common.h	2026-08-06 15:20:00
@@ -136,5 +136,7 @@
   char *airplay_device_model; // advertised model ("am="/"model=" TXT records and the AirPlay 2
                               // /info plist). Senders pick their device icon from this.
+  int airplay_third_party_speaker; // advertise feature bit 26 (Authentication_8, MFi): senders
+                                   // classify the receiver as a third-party (bookshelf) speaker.
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PA
   char *pa_server;           // the pulseaudio server address that Shairport Sync will play on.
--- a/shairport.c	2026-08-06 02:40:48
+++ b/shairport.c	2026-08-06 15:20:00
@@ -595,6 +595,17 @@
       if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_device_model", &str)) {
         config.airplay_device_model = (char *)str;
       }
+
+      /* Advertise AirPlay feature bit 26 (Authentication_8, MFi). Senders
+         classify a receiver with bit 26 (or 51) set as ThirdPartySpeaker and
+         draw the bookshelf-speaker icon for it; Apple model strings still
+         take precedence over the bit. */
+      config_set_lookup_bool(config.cfg, "general.airplay_third_party_speaker",
+                             &config.airplay_third_party_speaker);
+#ifdef CONFIG_AIRPLAY_2
+      if (config.airplay_third_party_speaker)
+        config.airplay_features |= ((uint64_t)1 << 26);
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_LIBDAEMON
       /* Get the Daemonize setting. */
       config_set_lookup_bool(config.cfg, "sessioncontrol.daemonize_with_pid_file", &daemonisewith);
